/**

@page page_exahype_main_function ExaHyPE's main function

\tableofcontents


As with any C++ code, every Peano 4 application needs exactly one file pair that hosts a `main()` function.
For a plain peano4.api.Project, this pair is produced by peano4.api.runner.DefaultSequence, but this default runner doesn't serve ExaHyPE as it is meant only to be a prototype.
So an ExaHyPE project defines its own runner. 
This is again an ExaHyPE-specific runner, but you can overwrite it with your own bespoke runner.
Bespoke runners come in handy, for example, if you want to have dedicated benchmark runs, or complex coupled solvers.


## Realisation

exahype2.api.Project realises its runner through aggregation: it holds a
`mainfile_generator` attribute, an instance of the nested abstract class
Project.Generator, whose `construct_output(peano_project)` is what actually
produces the main file pair. generate_Peano4_project() creates a fresh
peano4.api.Project, has every solver contribute its part, and only right
before it returns calls `self.mainfile_generator.construct_output(peano_project)` -
so the runner is the very last thing wired into the generated project.

peano4.api.Project itself has no notion of "runner": it just expects its
`main` attribute to be *some* object offering `construct_output(output,
main_name)`, and calls exactly that from generate(). This is a duck-typed
protocol, not a common base class. exahype2.api.DefaultSimulationMain
(a Project.Generator) realises this protocol via a small adapter,
`_ExaHyPEMainFileSequence`, and its own construct_output() does nothing more
than replace `peano_project.main` (which peano4.api.Project had already
defaulted to peano4.api.runner.DefaultSequence, itself a realisation of the
very same protocol) with that adapter. This is how the "aggregate that
produces a main" propagates across the two layers: an ExaHyPE-level
Generator swaps out a Peano4-level protocol implementation.

\dot
digraph ExaHyPEMainGeneration {
  rankdir=TB
  fontname="Helvetica"
  node [shape=record, fontname="Helvetica", fontsize=10]
  edge [fontname="Helvetica", fontsize=9]

  ExaProject     [label="{exahype2.api.Project|+ mainfile_generator : Project.Generator\l|+ generate_Peano4_project() : peano4.api.Project\l}"]
  Generator      [label="{«abstract»\nProject.Generator|+ project : Project\l|+ construct_output(peano_project) : void\l}"]
  DefaultSimMain [label="{exahype2.api.DefaultSimulationMain|+ construct_output(peano_project) : void\l}"]
  MainProtocol   [label="{«protocol»\nconstruct_output(output, main_name)}"]
  ExaMainSeq     [label="{exahype2.api._ExaHyPEMainFileSequence|+ HEADER_TEMPLATE : str\l+ CPP_TEMPLATE : str\l|+ construct_output(output, main_name) : void\l}"]
  DefaultSeq     [label="{peano4.api.runner.DefaultSequence|+ overwrite : bool\l|+ construct_output(output, main_name) : void\l}"]
  PeanoProject   [label="{peano4.api.Project|+ main : «protocol»\l|+ generate() : void\l}"]

  edge [arrowhead=empty, style=solid]
  DefaultSimMain -> Generator

  edge [arrowhead=empty, style=dashed]
  ExaMainSeq -> MainProtocol
  DefaultSeq -> MainProtocol

  edge [dir=both, arrowtail=diamond, arrowhead=none, style=solid]
  ExaProject -> Generator [taillabel="1", headlabel="1", label="mainfile_generator"]
  PeanoProject -> MainProtocol [taillabel="1", headlabel="1", label="main"]

  edge [dir=forward, arrowhead=vee, arrowtail=none, style=dashed]
  DefaultSimMain -> ExaMainSeq [label="«creates»,\nreplaces peano_project.main"]
  ExaProject -> PeanoProject [label="«creates»\ngenerate_Peano4_project()"]
}
\enddot

Solid hollow-triangle arrows are inheritance (DefaultSimulationMain extends
Project.Generator); dashed hollow-triangle arrows are realisation of the
duck-typed main-file protocol (by `_ExaHyPEMainFileSequence` and, by
default, `DefaultSequence`); diamond-ended lines are aggregation
(a Project holds exactly one such object); dashed open arrows are
"creates"/"replaces" dependencies at runtime. Reading the diagram
bottom-up: an ExaHyPE application never talks to `DefaultSequence` at all -
by the time peano4.api.Project.generate() runs, its `main` slot has already
been swapped out for the ExaHyPE-flavoured sequence.


